     "result_text_tail": "5M cash buffer, which sets the $7.5M cash target and the $3.5M funding trigger;\n  - the illustrative 25% and 50% rebid losses;\n  - the 0% (2028) and 20% (2030) specialty shares;\n  - the 13-week cash forecast.\n\n**Fidelity check.** I had an independent reviewer compare the finished deck with the analysis. No headline or gate number had changed. It did catch one real error: in shortening slide 10 I'd dropped \"within the molder's 2.5M ceiling\", so a bullet contradicted the chart next to it. I fixed that and restored several softened qualifiers, such as \"funding only plausible in 2028\" and \"up to 2 months\" of validation.\n\n**QA warnings I left in place:**\n- Nine slides are denser than the style guide likes. That's the source's density; trimming further would have meant dropping content.\n- Tables make up 8 of 19 content and appendix pages, as in the source.\n- Two sidebar numbers, the 4.6M break-even and the $0.6M deposit, are flagged as not computed from the exhibit next to them; both explain it.\n- One zero value has no formula.\n- The source-link check (`verify.py`) wasn't needed, because there are no web sources.\n\n**Calls I made without you:**\n- **Theme:** navy, the default.\n- **No section-divider slides.** The section tracker at the top of each slide does that job, and the slide order matches the source.\n- **The \"how we tested the answer\" slide sits under section 1.**\n\nIf you want, I can switch the theme or replace the analysis's proposed thresholds with values the committee sets."
